Root cause:
The bug was caused by a failure to properly manage the reference count of the device node (`comp->dev_node`) in the `mtk_mdp_comp_init` function. Specifically, when an error occurred during initialization (such as failing to get a clock or missing a required device node), the function did not call `of_node_put(comp->dev_node);` to decrement the reference count, leading to a potential memory leak and improper resource management. The patch added this call to ensure that the reference count is correctly managed on error paths.
